# Architecture

## Top-level layout

```
src/
  app/              # providers, navigation, bootstrap
  design/           # tokens, theme, primitives, motion, icons
  domain/           # pure logic (money, SMS rules, periods, budgets)
  db/               # SQLite, migrations, repositories, seed
  features/         # product features (home, transactions, analytics, …)
  lib/              # prefs, haptics, ids, notifications
  store/            # Zustand UI stores
  native/           # JS ↔ native bridges
```

## Rules

- Put product screens/hooks/components under `src/features/<feature>/`.
- Keep infrastructure (UI primitives, DB, domain, storage) outside `features/`.
- Keep app composition in `src/app`.
- Navigators should import feature screen entry points (barrel or `screens/`).
- Prefer local state; persist only UI prefs that need survival across launches.
- Do not create empty folders, placeholder screens, or nonexistent navigation routes.
- Android is primary for SMS; do not invent iOS SMS inbox APIs.
